# A ready extractor over a deposit, and no labor to work it.
#
# **Sean, 2026-09-17**: *I do want to make sure the extractors consume labor as well.* They always
# did - `work` has removed a labor since it was written - and nothing said so, which is the same
# shape of gap as the readiness one: a cost no test spends is a cost no test would notice losing.
#
# **The readiness is there**, which is what makes this about the labor.

